<Layout title="About the publication"><article class="reading wrap about"><p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p><h1>Make room for<br/><em>what matters.</em></h1><p class="article-intro">Useful advice should leave you with a clearer decision, not a longer to-do list.</p><h2>Three is a starting point</h2><p>Each guide focuses on three practical foundations for a specific goal. We add another when leaving it out would miss something essential. Numbers make the ideas easy to follow; they do not imply a universal scientific ranking.</p><h2 id="method">Evidence before certainty</h2><p>We compare possible recommendations by their likely impact, supporting evidence, practicality and distinct value. We favour authoritative guidance and research syntheses, and link sources to specific claims.</p><p>An association does not establish cause. A recommendation from a respected institution is not a guarantee. Where evidence is limited or circumstances change the advice, we say so.</p><h2>How AI contributes</h2><p>AI assists with research, drafting and development. Our publication policy requires a separate editorial and factual review before release. This preview contains draft articles; independent review has not yet been completed.</p><p>Source notes distinguish the pages we could check from material we could not access. Automated checks can find missing fields and broken links; they cannot establish that advice is sound.</p><h2>Corrections and revisions</h2><p>Meaningful revisions keep the original publication date and show a revision date. Advice that becomes materially misleading is withdrawn while it is corrected. Publication frequency never takes priority over resolving significant problems.</p><h2>General guidance, with limits</h2><p>These articles are educational. They cannot account for your health, finances, family circumstances or local rules. Important qualifications stay visible, rather than being hidden in expandable detail.</p><h2>A quiet publication</h2><p>No accounts, advertising, affiliate links or paid content. The working name and visual identity may change; the aim is to keep the publication useful and trustworthy.</p></article></Layout>
